// MC-PATCH: write-empty-content-allowed-v1
	// REPLACE: 		label: "content"
	// Lesson 1424 (2026-10-22, David): MC's `write` tool rejected empty-string
	// content with "Missing required parameter: content (received: path,
	// content=<empty-string>)". Reproduced verbatim in the rc57.27 sidecar log
	// while the model was scaffolding a Python package:
	//   email_assistant/__init__.py  content:""
	// An empty file is a legitimate request (empty __init__.py, a placeholder,
	// a template stub). The model was CORRECT; the validator was wrong.
	//
	// Why this is the right fix, not a workaround: the upstream framework
	// ALREADY has an `allowEmpty` flag on required-param groups, honored in
	// three places in this same bundle:
	//   1. assertRequiredParams()  -> `if (group.allowEmpty) return true;`
	//   2. formatReceivedParamHint() -> suppresses the `<empty-string>` hint
	//   3. describeReceivedParamValue(value, allowEmpty)
	// It was simply never set for the `write` group. So this is a one-flag
	// opt-in, not new logic.
	//
	// Blast radius (verified by extracting the real functions from the bundle
	// and running 11 assertions, all passing):
	//   - content:"" / "\n" / "# docstring"  -> now ACCEPTED (the fix)
	//   - content missing / content:null    -> still REJECTED
	//   - path missing / path:""             -> still REJECTED (unchanged)
	//   - read + edit tools                  -> completely unchanged
	// `path` is deliberately NOT allowEmpty — an empty path is never valid.
	//
	// Related but separate: the "Tool loop did not produce an answer" 3-retry
	// failure in the same log is a DIFFERENT bug (Lesson 1423 / MAIC
	// tool_execution body) and is NOT addressed here.
		label: "content", allowEmpty: !0